<Layout title="Membership | Kin & Campus">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Membership</div><h1>A hundred and nineteen a month while they're on campus.</h1><p class="lead">One seat for the academic year. A local pediatrician who already knows them.</p></div>
<div class="w"><div class="price"><div class="card"><h3>School year</h3><div class="big">$119/mo</div><p>August through May. Direct access, visits, check-ins, a letter home.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Academic year</h3><div class="big">$1,190</div><p>Billed once for August–May, or $119 a month for ten months.</p></div></div><p class="note">Membership is not health insurance. Keep coverage for labs, specialists, and emergencies.</p></div>
<section><div class="w"><h2 style="margin-bottom:20px">Questions parents ask</h2>
<details><summary>What does membership include?</summary><p>Unlimited office visits, usually same day. Direct physician text. Wellness check-ins around holidays, finals, and the week back from break. Letters to the hometown physician. Medication continuity. Forms for travel, housing, and athletics.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will you share my student's information with me?</summary><p>You get the standing rule you agree on. At 18 the chart is theirs. We write it down and follow it. Their hometown doctor gets the note the same afternoon.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does this replace insurance?</summary><p>No. Membership is not insurance. Keep your student's coverage for labs, specialists, and emergencies.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if my student is away from Blacksburg?</summary><p>In-person care in Blacksburg is the core. Tele visits when a room is not required.</p></details>
<details><summary>What if it's an emergency?</summary><p>Call 911 or go to the nearest emergency room. Then let us know in the morning, and we'll help with follow-up.</p></details></div></section>
</Layout>
